I don't know about anyone else, but I've been reading Dave's
rumors on the bottom line now for a while, and I think they're at least
as good as the real ones.

I originally wanted to move that his rumors be added to the rumors file
since it repeats a little too often.

However, as I read through yet more of these elegant works of art
(riding that balance between humor and fact) I have come up with a
better idea.

Make a new game character and scroll type. "Dave the Editor" and "Dave's
Discourse" - a scroll of news!

A scroll of news is a collection of say 3 or 4 of Dave's rumors (as
distinguished from those "other" rumors.) Obviously, the news option
would be "#define NEWS" so there's room to expand on this paper a bit,
with headlines like "Wiz swings big at 38th party" "Lorelin removes
clothes in public!"

Second, we have the wandering character, Dave the Editor, running around
delivering his newspaper. If you #chat with him, he'll sell you the
paper for a gold piece (paper's not cheap in the dungeon.) If you pay
him perhaps a bit more, he mighttoss out a few more worthwhile gems.
Dave might even make mention of things to come, say "Just was talking
to Mr. Conklin" (the ghost on the next level) or "Watch that
cockatrice"

Of course, we'll need access to the Dave rumor archive.

